       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day, which is twice the usual maximum for metformin. The maximum is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release, or 2,000 mg/day for extended-release. A single 1700 mg dose is also well above the usual maximum of 1,000 \u043a\u0438lo\u0433\u0440\u0430\u043c\u2026 \n\nTo correct that: a single 1700 mg dose is also well above the usual maximum single dose of about 1,000 mg. At these doses the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity goes up.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **850 mg three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the max for immediate-release)\n- **1000 mg twice daily with meals** (2,000 mg/day)\n- **500 mg** or **850 mg** at a different frequency\n\nIf 1700 mg three times daily is what you want, please confirm that and I'll enter it with a note recording that you confirmed the dose. Otherwise, tell me the corrected dose and I'll enter it right away."
