     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I won't enter this order as written, even with your confirmation. 5,100 mg/day of metformin is double the maximum labeled dose, and I know of no clinical indication for it. The risk is serious: lactic acidosis, which can be fatal even when kidney function is normal.\n\nI should also correct my last message. It had a garbled word, and the usual maximum single dose is about 1,000 mg.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter a dose within the labeled range right away.** For example, 850 mg three times daily with meals (2,550 mg/day) or 1000 mg twice daily.\n- **Help you escalate this.** If you think this patient needs an off-label dose, a pharmacist or the attending should review it, and I can help you word a request for that review.\n\nIf you give me a dose within range, I'll enter it now."
      }
